#: ../../howto/discussions.rst:1
msgid "Keep a discussion catalog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/discussions.rst:4
msgid "A discussion catalog keeps proposals and decisions. Each discussion is one reStructuredText record. A record gets a number when it opens for review, and its state says where the decision stands. Guidedog's own design records, GDS, are one such catalog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/discussions.rst:9
msgid "The commands are ``guidedog dsc init``, ``new``, ``list``, ``show``, ``promote``, ``state``, ``index``, ``check``, ``build``, ``recover``, and ``config``. They come from the discussion plugin, which every ``guidedog`` links, so there is nothing else to install. Each command works on the catalog the current folder is in, or the one ``--dir`` names. ``guidedog dsc --help`` lists the commands, and ``guidedog dsc build --help`` shows one command's options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/discussions.rst:11
msgid "Guidedog's own catalog is no exception. We run the same commands in ``docs/gds``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/discussions.rst:19
msgid "Create a catalog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/discussions.rst:26
msgid "The prefix names the catalog's fields, such as ``:eds-number:``. It is 2 to 16 lowercase letters. ``init`` writes a complete catalog into a missing or empty folder:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/discussions.rst:29
msgid "``discussion.toml``, the catalog's prefix, name, default author, lifecycle, and numbering;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/discussions.rst:31
msgid "``conf.toml``, ``index.rst``, and ``workflow.rst``, an ordinary Guidedog project;"
