#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:76
msgid "Confirm that ``source_suffix`` lists every extension we use (for example, ``[\".rst\", \".md\"]``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:77
msgid "Check that ``exclude_patterns`` excludes build folders, virtual environments, and temporary files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:78
msgid "Run a quick semantic check using the dummy builder:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:84
msgid "The dummy builder checks every document and link without writing HTML files. We fix each warning about a missing document or a malformed include."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:87
msgid "Pass 2: Verify references, domains, and custom objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:90
msgid "Next, we verify that cross-references and domain directives resolve:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:92
msgid "**Standard domains:** Guidedog supports the standard Python, C, C++, and JavaScript domains, with their roles such as ``:py:func:``, ``:c:type:``, and ``:cpp:class:``. It adds ``odin`` and ``rust`` domains of its own (see :doc:`../topics/domains`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:95
msgid "**Intersphinx links:** If our Sphinx project linked to external documentation through Intersphinx, we keep our ``[intersphinx_mapping]`` in ``conf.toml``. Guidedog fetches and parses standard ``objects.inv`` files itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:98
msgid "**Declarative custom object types:** In Sphinx, projects often wrote small Python extensions that call ``app.add_object_type()`` to create custom directives and roles (such as ``.. confval::`` or ``.. setting::``). In Guidedog, we declare these in ``conf.toml`` under ``[[object_types]]``, without code. See :doc:`../object-types`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:103
msgid "Pass 3: Verify presentation and templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:106
msgid "Finally, we check how the output looks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:108
msgid "**HTML website:** Run ``guidedog build html path/to/docs -W`` and inspect the generated pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:109
msgid "**Jinja templates:** Guidedog's native Jinja engine supports block inheritance:"
